# centered-window — system overview
# A two-part hack for borderless windowed SoF: a Python probe writes the real
# work-area height once, and a SoFplus script centres the window from it.
# Zones run left to right: entry points -> core -> state -> external.
# Style classes set strokes only, so light and dark stay readable.

title: |md
  # centered-window
  A Python probe plus a SoFplus addon that make a borderless windowed SoF sit in the middle of the Windows work area.
| {near: top-center}

direction: right
grid-columns: 2
grid-rows: 2
horizontal-gap: 150
vertical-gap: 110

entry: Entry points {
  direction: down

  bat: `install_center_window.bat` · runs the probe from the SoF folder, then `start SoF.exe`
  py: `center_window.py` · the only thing that asks Windows where the taskbar is
  func: `sofplus/addons/centered_window.func` · runs inside the game at map load
}

core: Core {
  direction: down

  dpi: choose DPI mode · Win10 `SetProcessDpiAwareness(2)`, Win7 `SetProcessDPIAware`, any other release `sys.exit(1)`
  probe: read work area · `GetMonitorInfo(MonitorFromPoint(0,0))`, the bottom edge is the screen minus the taskbar
  once: write once · create `sofplus/data/cw_work_area.cfg` only if the file does not exist
  init: read both resolutions · split `_sp_cl_vid_mode_0` on `:` and `vid_mode_` + `gl_mode` on `x`
  border: force borderless · if `_sp_cl_vid_border` is 1, set 0 and `vid_restart`
  wait: wait for the cfg · 1 s timer execs the file, and retries every second with an `echo` hint until `cw_res_desktop_y` is set
  center: centre it · half desktop minus half game size, written to `vid_xpos` and `vid_ypos`

  dpi -> probe: without awareness the taskbar height is wrong
  probe -> once: one integer, the work-area bottom
  init -> border: cvars only, no file
  border -> wait: the restart must finish first
  wait -> center: one more 1 ms timer
}

state: State {
  direction: down

  cfg: `sofplus/data/cw_work_area.cfg` · one `set` line, written once {shape: cylinder}
  cvars: `cw_res_desktop_x`, `cw_res_desktop_y`, `cw_res_sof_x`, `cw_res_sof_y` plus two tilde-prefixed scratch cvars · session only
}

ext: External {
  direction: down

  windows: Win32 · `GetMonitorInfo`, `MonitorFromPoint`, DPI shcore, the taskbar itself
  game: SoF.exe · reads `vid_xpos` and `vid_ypos` when it creates the window
  sofplus: SoFplus scripting · `sp_sc_cvar_*`, `sp_sc_timer`, `sp_sc_flow_if`
}

entry -> core: the bat runs the probe, the addon runs the maths
core -> state: the probe leaves one number, the addon leaves cvars
core -> ext: Windows answers once, the game and SoFplus consume

classes: {
  entry: {style: {stroke: "#2f6fbf"}}
  core: {style: {stroke: "#2f8f5f"}}
  state: {style: {stroke: "#a86a12"; stroke-dash: 3}}
  ext: {style: {stroke: "#8a4fbf"; stroke-dash: 5}}
}

entry.class: entry
core.class: core
state.class: state
ext.class: ext
